Carafe bench: a 39-bit process's code starts at 64 GiB instead of 2 GiB.
Without ASLR every region is laid out right after the code, so the 64 GiB kernel map region, where thread
local pages go, began inside the low 4 GiB. A 32-bit guest that reserves that window (Wine with WOW64) then
left no room for thread local pages and thread creation failed with OutOfMemory after a few threads. 4 GiB is
not far enough either: Wine maps fixed addresses just above it. On the console the regions are placed at
random across the address space, all far above the low 4 GiB.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the file it changes.

--- a/src/core/hle/kernel/k_process.cpp
+++ b/src/core/hle/kernel/k_process.cpp
@@ -1210,7 +1210,7 @@
         // existence of ASLR pages before the entry point, so we will adjust the load address
         // to point to about 2GiB into the ASLR region.
         flag |= Svc::CreateProcessFlag::AddressSpace64Bit;
-        code_address = 0x8000'0000 + aslr_space_offset;
+        code_address = 0x10'0000'0000 + aslr_space_offset;
         break;
     case FileSys::ProgramAddressSpaceType::Is36Bit:
         flag |= Svc::CreateProcessFlag::AddressSpace64BitDeprecated;
